{
  "id": "07316_rifujin",
  "headword": "{理不尽|りふじん}",
  "reading": "りふじん",
  "part_of_speech": "na-adjective",
  "gloss": "unreasonable; unjust; unfair",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "unreasonable; unjust; unfair",
      "explanation": "Going against reason or fairness; irrational and difficult to accept."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "07316_rifujin_ex1",
      "japanese": "{理不尽|りふじん}な{要求|ようきゅう}に{困|こま}っている。",
      "english": "I'm troubled by unreasonable demands.",
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "07316_rifujin_ex2",
      "japanese": "なぜ{私|わたし}だけ{怒|おこ}られるのか{理不尽|りふじん}だ。",
      "english": "It's unfair that only I get scolded.",
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "07316_rifujin_ex3",
      "japanese": "{理不尽|りふじん}な{扱|あつか}いに{抗議|こうぎ}した。",
      "english": "I protested the unfair treatment.",
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    }
  ],
  "notes": "FORMS:\n{理|り} (reason) + {不尽|ふじん} (not exhaustive, lacking) → lacking reason = unreasonable\n- {理不尽|りふじん}な{要求|ようきゅう} - unreasonable demand\n- {理不尽|りふじん}な{扱|あつか}い - unfair treatment\n- {理不尽|りふじん}さ (noun) - unreasonableness\n\nUSAGE:\n{理不尽|りふじん} expresses strong feelings about something that violates basic fairness or logic. Often used when someone feels wronged or sees injustice.\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {不条理|ふじょうり} - absurd, irrational\n- {無理|むり} - unreasonable (less formal)\n- {横暴|おうぼう} - tyrannical, overbearing",
